<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulf of Aden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gulf of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> is an arm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a>, linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. Its ports, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a>, were vital outlets for trade from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-highlands">Ethiopian highlands</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> drew much of its wealth and political orientation from its position along this coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden.jpg" alt="Gulf of Aden" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Space Agency · CC BY-SA 3.0 igo · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Envisat_image_of_the_Gulf_of_Aden_ESA219526.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
